The purpose of this project is for me to practice my ability programming using the following tools:

JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Node.js, NPM, Web Components, Lit, Vite, Git, Bash

There is absolutely no AI generated code of any kind allowed in this project. All AI coding tools are banned.
Also no copying and pasting chunks of code from any external source into this project.

Steps:
1. Set up git for this project, making it a repository.
2. Write the node.js server shell.
3. Write a test for each server endpoint.
4. Make an HTML page and have it served at GET /.
5. Update tests to check all pages.
6. Implement hot reload of page via WebSocket.
7. Write tests for the WebSocket.
8. Add functionality to make buttons on page work.
9. Add a global chat to the server.
10. Write POST, PATCH, DELETE, GET and write tests for all.
11. Export start server functionality and make test file start the server.
12. Expand tests to cover WebSocket behavior.
13. Test file should use its own data file and perhaps each test should clear the file.
14. Refactor file server and ensure it's secure.
15. Write a fetch wrapper and refactor test file to use it.
16. Start designing UI and breaking it up into a component library.
17. Write a WebSocket wrapper and refactor test file to monitor the socket throughout the tests.
18. Ensure browser can get the shared modules.
19. Write tests for the UI itself, meaning simulate inputs and clicks, I think.
20. Server needs to assign a user id to each client and associate messages with users.
21. Continuously refactor UI into a tree of components, should become continuously more declarative.
22. Write client store for messages state.
23. Update file server to support expanded client.
24. Refactor such that expected cwd is project root.

Notes:
- Should write pipeline that runs the integration tests and ensures they pass
- Consider making the tests start and stop the server












